<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Intentionally empty for the local-only MVP (851-2402, 851-2400):

	- No App Sandbox. The app is Developer ID-distributed, not Mac App Store, so
	  sandboxing (and the app-group container it would require to share the vault
	  DB with LilPasswordsAgent) buys nothing here. App and helper share a plain
	  directory instead; see docs/adr/0001-storage-and-process-model.md.
	- No keychain-access-groups. Only LilPasswordsAgent touches the Keychain
	  (legacy file-based keychain, no entitlement required); the app and lilpass
	  never read the vault key directly, so there is nothing to share an access
	  group with. keychain-access-groups is also a *restricted* entitlement:
	  AMFI kills a process that carries it without a matching provisioning
	  profile, which we don't have until the 851 Labs Apple Developer team
	  exists (see 851-2400).
	- No iCloud entitlements, per the project's local-first decision.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
